; The port's library, wrapped as Seekwright: the module a test or bin/ refers
; to as [Seekwright.Model] is [lib/model.ml]. The Python tree's own src/ is not
; part of this workspace.
;
; The provider adapters are NOT in this library: they sit in [lib/providers/],
; which carries its own stanza because [(include_subdirs qualified)] here would
; forbid the [lib/caps/] stanza that defines mcp-caps. The direction is the one
; that matters — [seekwright.providers] depends on this library and nothing here
; depends on it, so the engine holds [Seekwright.Provider.t] values without ever
; naming an adapter.
;
; [yojson] is the wire codec (P2), [toml] the config file's parser (P3),
; [mcp-caps] and [uri] the provider seam (P4): a provider adapter reaches its
; endpoint only through a [Mcp_caps.Authority.Net] grant, and [uri] names that
; endpoint. [digestif] is [hashlib.sha256] for the [qhash] correlation handle the
; engine binds (P5). The routing core [router] (P1) is stdlib-only by design — not
; by the absence of a [libraries] field (these are here for other modules) but by
; the [ocamldep] diff in test/dune, which pins the router's dependencies and fails
; runtest if it reaches for any sibling module.
(library
 (name seekwright)
 (public_name seekwright)
 (libraries digestif mcp-caps eio toml uri yojson))

